														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2389713">
									

<p>Let's see how this one goes. This was a tricky one to write. I tried making other changes to it past this point, but those left me unsatisfied. This one was originally an idea for the Short Story Contest that was shelved in favor of <a href="/scp-2810">SCP-2810</a> and revived. Thanks to Cavalry, Cyclopian, Drazool, DreamwalkerFae, polearms, psul, rumetzen, and probably others for feedback.</p>
<p>Also grudging thanks to Decibelles, Lex1nat0r, and TwistedGears for telling me to fundamentally alter the original concept of this one (guess what tho I didn't delete it so eat it).</p>
<p>See more of my work on my <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/dr-arvind-desais-personnel-file">author page</a>!</p>
<p>Image sourcing for SQUID.JPG:<br />
<a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teuthowenia_megalops_(Michael_Vecchione,_NOAA).jpg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teuthowenia_megalops_(Michael_Vecchione,_NOAA).jpg</a> -<br />
<strong>Closeup of the eyes of Teuthowenia megalops (ventral view). The three photophores are visible on each eye (light yellow-golden areas)</strong>. <a href="https://www.nefsc.noaa.gov/press_release/2008/SciSpot/ss0810/">Michael Vecchione, NOAA Fisheries Service.</a><br />
<em>This image is in the public domain because it contains materials that originally came from the U.S. National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration, taken or made as part of an employee's official duties.</em></p>

