					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/decibelles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2005044); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2005044&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607930425" alt="Decibelles" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2005044)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/decibelles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2005044); return false;" >Decibelles</a></span> <span class="odate time_1444541987 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Oct 2015 05:39</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2389839">
									

<p>When we're going for something that not only is hazardous enough to infect a whole site, but <em>does</em> infect a whole site, it better be at a level of OTT enough to do so. <a href="/scp-2690">SCP-2690</a> does this via religious means (though I wasn't much of a fan otherwise), and 1561 piled it on as the article went on.</p>
<p>The goofy lovey-dovey tone doesn't do it favors, because, and maybe it's me, once we see something so saccharine and sweet, our indicators go off and we sense something is fucked. In addition, we get the idea very soon that oh hey, they grafted its skin onto theirs. This isn't subtle, but tries to present it as gradual and subtle. And that does no favors for me, because this would be so much better if it were going the extra steps to make this OTT.</p>
<p>Also, as a final note, <em>there's no reason to not neutralize it</em>. Say what you want about the Foundation; this is a large-scale containment breach, and it doesn't take much for this to potentially spill out into something far more dangerous. 2690 uses the religious motivators as a means to not neutralize this, and 1561&#8230; well, they want to, but can't. But there's no other reasons here. And any excuse for the Foundation to not be aware of it is dashed by the note at the end (and nothing to indicate they took care of the problem), which breaks my disbelief.</p>

							</div>

								
					
